{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Truly.</b> Then they will give thanks to HaShem and say: It is true that You are an El who hides from the nation, in whom You have no desire, and You are the Elohim of Israel, their savior. The commentators said that מסתתר is like נסתר, and it appears [so] because of Israel, whom You saved. But this is not correct grammatically, for מסתתר is of the hitpa'el binyan."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:10.023689097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}